roy: Durai, walking in at 6.15. As usual.
durai: God, is it that late already? I'm not super eager to get out there. I don't know if I can really, "perform", in this cold weather...
roy: Doesn't all true art rely on inherent suffering? Your mascot suit is thick. You'll obviously be fine...
Durai leaves
durai: OH, HELLO YOUNG MAN! GEE, YOUR CLOTHES LOOK DIRTY! WHY NOT COME IN AND BUY SOME LAUNDRY DETERGENT?
durai: AH, SOME GENTLEMEN ON A NIGHT OUT! I KNOW ALL ABOUT NIGHTS OUT - MY FAMILY, BACK IN SAVINGSLAND, USED TO -
durai: SIR, THAT'S JUST NOT A VERY NICE THING TO SAY. YEAH OF COURSE YOU FIND IT FUNNY.
durai: UM, YOU THERE, MA'AM! PERHAPS YOU'RE OUT LATE TO GO SEE A MOVIE? WHY NOT COME IN AND BUY SOME POPCORN... UM, OKAY!
Durai enters
durai: Gosh... tough crowd out there today.
roy: Mm. Totally.
roy: Durai, you know, I think you shouldn't rib into the people who seem down on their luck.
roy: ...I mean, when I used to be homeless, I carried a knife.
durai: "Used to be homeless"... are you not homeless now?
durai: I just always thought you were.
durai: Like you're always working. I remember when I started I thought "Gee, he must really need this."
roy: Mm. Nope. Not homeless anymore.
roy: Say, Durai. I heard that Oleysa said it'd be a good idea to list out all our stock alphabetically, so people can just listen and check if we have what they need.
durai: Oleysa said that?!
durai: She's hardly ever taken an interest to Breadsworth. I guess I could give it a shot!
durai: See you in a bit, Roy!
Durai leaves
durai: GEE, WE HAVE SO MUCH IN STOCK TODAY!
durai: APPLES... ASPARAGUS... AUBERGINE... AVOCADOS... 
game: Durai's tactic confused passerbies more than anything. Roy seemed to enjoy frustrating him, but Durai didn't bring in the customers like he usually does. Bad shift.